200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="town-b"><h2 class="town-h">Waterbury</h2><small>New Haven County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/ct-towns/norwalk/"><img class="town-img" src="/assets/img/photos/rowayton-marina.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/rowayton-marina-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/rowayton-marina.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 50vw, 25vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="town-b"><h2 class="town-h">Norwalk</h2><small>Fairfield County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/ct-towns/danbury/"><img class="town-img" src="/assets/img/photos/candlewood-lake.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/candlewood-lake-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/candlewood-lake.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 50vw, 25vw" width="1200" height="719" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="town-b"><h2 class="town-h">Danbury</h2><small>Fairfield County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/ct-towns/new-london/"><img class="town-img" src="/assets/img/photos/new-london-harbor.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/new-london-harbor-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/new-london-harbor.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 50vw, 25vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="town-b"><h2 class="town-h">New London</h2><small>New London County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/ct-towns/greenwich/"><img class="town-img" src="/assets/img/photos/rowayton-boathouse.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/rowayton-boathouse-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/rowayton-boathouse.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 50vw, 25vw" width="1200" height="899" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="town-b"><h2 class="town-h">Greenwich</h2><small>Fairfield County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/ct-towns/west-hartford/"><img class="town-img" src="/assets/img/photos/fallen-tree.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/fallen-tree-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/fallen-tree.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 50vw, 25vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="town-b"><h2 class="town-h">West Hartford</h2><small>Hartford County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/ct-towns/milford/"><img class="town-img" src="/assets/img/photos/milford-point.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/milford-point-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/milford-point.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 50vw, 25vw" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="town-b"><h2 class="town-h">Milford</h2><small>New Haven County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/ct-towns/torrington/"><img class="town-img" src="/assets/img/photos/winter-farm.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/winter-farm-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/winter-farm.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 50vw, 25vw" width="960" height="637" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="town-b"><h2 class="town-h">Torrington</h2><small>Litchfield County</small></span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="sec sec-tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head rv"><p class="kicker">Regions</p><h2>How claims differ across Connecticut</h2><p>Connecticut abolished county government in 1960, but its eight counties, Fairfield, Hartford, Litchfield, Middlesex, New Haven, New London, Tolland and Windham, are still how most people describe where they live. The same policy reads very differently on the shoreline and in the hills.</p><ul class="chips chips-center"><li>Fairfield</li><li>Hartford</li><li>Litchfield</li><li>Middlesex</li><li>New Haven</li><li>New London</li><li>Tolland</li><li>Windham</li></ul></div><div class="icards" data-stagger><div class="icard rv"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/rowayton-marina.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/rowayton-marina-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/rowayton-marina.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k">Greenwich · Stamford · Norwalk · Bridgeport</span><h3>Fairfield County &amp; the Gold Coast</h3><p>Waterfront homes from Byram to Black Rock face Long Island Sound, while backcountry estates sit under tall oaks. Sandy and Isaias left both kinds of damage.</p></span></div><div class="icard rv"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/hartford-river.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/hartford-river-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/hartford-river.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1200" height="726" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k">Hartford · West Hartford · Manchester</span><h3>Greater Hartford</h3><p>The Capitol Region’s older housing, from Asylum Hill Victorians to West Hartford colonials, makes plaster, slate and matching the usual sticking points.</p></span></div><div class="icard rv"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/milford-point.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/milford-point-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/milford-point.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k">New Haven · Milford · Guilford · Old Saybrook</span><h3>New Haven &amp; the Shoreline</h3><p>From the 1989 Hamden tornado to Irene and Sandy on Milford’s beaches, the central shoreline sees wind from every direction.</p></span></div><div class="icard rv"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/winter-valley.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/winter-valley-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/winter-valley.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k">Waterbury · Danbury · Naugatuck · Shelton</span><h3>Naugatuck &amp; Housatonic Valleys</h3><p>Inland valleys see more summer hail than the coast and harsher winters. Brick mills and hillside three-deckers add their own complications.</p></span></div><div class="icard rv"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/winter-farm.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/winter-farm-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/winter-farm.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 100vw, 33vw" width="960" height="637" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k">Torrington · Litchfield · New Milford · Winsted</span><h3>Litchfield Hills</h3><p>Higher ground means heavier snow, longer freezes and more seasonal homes, so heat, vacancy and collapse wording all come into play.</p></span></div><div class="icard rv"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/new-london-harbor.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/new-london-harbor-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/new-london-harbor.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:640px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k">New London · Groton · Norwich · Willimantic</span><h3>Eastern Connecticut &amp; the Quiet Corner</h3><p>The 1938 hurricane hit New London hardest. Today the region mixes shoreline exposure, historic downtowns and rural homes on large lots.</p></span></div></div></div></section>
<section class="cta-strip"><div class="wrap cta-strip-in rv"><div><h2>Don’t see your town?</h2><p>We cover all 169. Call and tell us where the property is.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-coral" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/contact-ct-appraiser/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
